{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Old_Beggar","to":"Old Beggar"},{"from":"Golden_Idol_(Event)","to":"Golden Idol (Event)"},{"from":"Designer_In-Spire","to":"Designer In-Spire"},{"from":"Secret_Portal","to":"Secret Portal"},{"from":"Forgotten_Altar","to":"Forgotten Altar"},{"from":"The_Woman_in_Blue","to":"The Woman in Blue"},{"from":"The_Divine_Fountain","to":"The Divine Fountain"},{"from":"Tomb_of_Lord_Red_Mask","to":"Tomb of Lord Red Mask"},{"from":"Upgrade_Shrine","to":"Upgrade Shrine"},{"from":"The_Nest","to":"The Nest"},{"from":"Council_of_Ghosts","to":"Council of Ghosts"},{"from":"The_Colosseum","to":"The Colosseum"},{"from":"Golden_Shrine","to":"Golden Shrine"},{"from":"The_Joust","to":"The Joust"},{"from":"The_Library","to":"The Library"},{"from":"Bonfire_Spirits","to":"Bonfire Spirits"}],"pages":{"3196":{"pageid":3196,"ns":0,"title":"Augmenter","revisions":[{"revid":55306,"parentid":54575,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Augmenter\n|Image=Event-Augmenter.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Mutagenic Strength}} {{Small Card Infobox|J.A.X.}}\n{{E|Augmenter}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. This Event is the only way to obtain {{C|J.A.X.}} and {{R|Mutagenic Strength}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Test J.A.X.}} {{TS|positive||Get JAXXED.}}\n* Adds {{C|J.A.X.}} to the player's deck.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Become Test Subject}} {{TS|positive||[[Transform]] 2 cards.}}\n* Read more on Transform rules [[Transform#Rules|here]].\n<br>\n{{Frame|Ingest Mutagens}} {{TS|positive|| Obtain a special relic.}} \n* Rewards the player with {{R|Mutagenic Strength}}.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nA man with an eyepatch and a devilish grin strides up to you.\n<br>\n\"Hey there, stranger. Interested in advancing science? I can make you stronger than any training or blessing. You're gonna need it if you're one of those heroes with a death wish.\"\n<br><br>\n{{TS||up|\"Whad'ya say?\"}}\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Test J.A.X.}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||up|\"Excellent.\"}}\n<br>\nThe man hands over a dangerous looking syringe filled with a {{TS|blue|up|glowing liquid}} before skulking off into a shadowy alleyway.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Become Test Subject}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||up|\"Marvelous.\"}}\n<br>\nYou quaff the mysterious substance. Immediately, you are invigorated and feel your muscle fibers {{TS||shake|twitch.}}\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Ingest Mutagens}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||up|\"Superb.\"}}\n<br>\nThe man injects you with three unknown substances and pulls out a notepad. As you begin to feel light-headed, he starts to frantically write down notes.\n<br>\nLosing track of time completely, by the time you regain your senses, the shady character has disappeared.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Augmenter was originally called \"J.A.X. Dealer\". It was renamed because, early into Slay the Spire's development, {{E|Pleading Vagrant}} previously accepted {{C|J.A.X.}} from the J.A.X. Dealer but was reworked to accept 85 [[Gold]] instead. Following the change, the old name no longer made sense and had to also be changed. It could have also been changed due to the negative connotations of the word \"dealer\".\n* Internally called <code>Drug_Dealer</code>.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Minor text cleanup for Augmenter event.\n** Typo fix in Augmenter event.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 46: Adrenaline'''\n** Fixed punctuation in Augmenter event.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 44: Chrysalis'''\n** Augmenter event transform option now allows choosing 2 cards to Transform instead of selecting 3 at random.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Augmenter event no longer incorrectly upgrades transformed cards.\n** Augmenter event will no longer give out duplicate relics on Endless mode.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** J.A.X Dealer event reworked.\n** J.A.X. Dealer event renamed -> Augmenter.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** J.A.X. Dealer event's cost of J.A.X. updated 100 -> 77 Gold.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Incorrectly using wavy text in JAX event fixed.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3058":{"pageid":3058,"ns":0,"title":"Bonfire Spirits","revisions":[{"revid":54538,"parentid":45964,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Bonfire Spirits\n|Image=Event-BonfireSpirits.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Spirit Poop}}\n{{E|Bonfire Spirits}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Offer}} Receive a reward based on the offer.\n* Offer a card in your deck to remove. The reward you receive depends on the rarity of the card you give.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<i>You happen upon what looks like a group of {{TS|purple||purple fire spirits}} {{TS||up|dancing}} around a large bonfire.</i>\n\nBefore selecting {{Frame|Offer}}\n<blockquote>\n<i>The spirits toss small bones and fragments into the fire, which {{TS||up|brilliantly erupts}} each time.</i><br>\n<i>As you approach, the spirits all turn to you, expectantly...</i>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Offer}}\n<blockquote>\n<i>You toss an offering into the bonfire.</i>\n\nWhen offering a {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} card\n<blockquote>\n<i>Nothing happens...</i><br>\n<i>The spirits seem to be ignoring you now. Disappointing...</i>\n</blockquote>\n\nWhen offering a {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} card\n<blockquote>\n<i>The flames grow slightly brighter.</i><br>\n<i>The spirits continue dancing. You feel slightly warmer from their presence..</i><br>\n<i>You {{TS|green||heal}} {{TS|blue||5}} HP.</i>\n</blockquote>\n\nWhen offering an {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} card\n<blockquote>\n<i>The flames erupt, growing significantly stronger!</i><br>\n<i>The spirits dance around you excitedly, filling you with a {{TS||up|sense of warmth.}}</i><br>\n<i>You are {{TS|green||healed}} to full HP.</i>\n</blockquote>\n\nWhen offering a {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} card\n<blockquote>\n<i>The flames {{TS||shake|burst}}, nearly knocking you off your feet, as the fire {{TS||shake|doubles}} in strength.</i><br>\n<i>The spirits dance around you excitedly before {{TS||up|merging into your form,}} filling you with warmth and strength.</i><br>\n<i>Your Max HP increases by {{TS|blue||10}} and you are {{TS|green||healed}} to full HP.</i>\n</blockquote>\n\nWhen offering a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}}\n<blockquote>\n<i>However, the spirits aren't happy you offered a {{TS|purple||Curse...}}</i><br>\n<i>The card fizzles a meek black smoke. You receive a... {{TS|purple|up|something}} in return.</i><br>\n(Gives {{R|Spirit Poop}})\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* This event treats {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Basic|Basic}} cards as a lower rarity than {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}}.\n* Obtaining {{R|Spirit Poop}} adds the '''Poopy''' [[Score]] bonus which lowers your total score by one.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"1764":{"pageid":1764,"ns":0,"title":"Council of Ghosts","revisions":[{"revid":55405,"parentid":54576,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Council of Ghosts\n|Image=Event-Ghosts.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Apparition}}\n{{E|Council of Ghosts}} is an event found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Accept}} {{TS|positive||Receive 5}} {{Asc|15|(3)}} {{C|Apparition|Apparitions}}. {{TS|negative||Lose X Max HP.}}\n* X is equal to 50% of the player's Max HP, rounded up.\n\n{{Frame|Refuse}} Nothing happens.\n<br>\n<br>\nYou are then given the option to {{Frame|Leave}}.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">As you continue your ascent, {{TS|purple|up|thick black smoke}} begins to billow out of the ground and walls around you, coalescing into three masked forms that start to speak.\n\n<br>\n{{TS||up|\"Another puppet of }} {{TS|gold|up|Neow}} {{TS||up| I think.\"}}<br>\n{{TS|red|shake|\"AGREED! SHE ALWAYS MAKES THE FUNNEST TOYS!\"}}\n\n\nYou notice an over-sized grin as the third addresses you.\n\"Ignore the others... Would you like a taste of our {{TS|gold|up|power?\"}}</div>\n\n{{Frame|Accept}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS|gold||\"Excellent!\"}}\n\nAs the ghostly shape speaks, you notice its large mouth opening wider and wider. {{TS|purple|up|Thick black smoke}} spews forth and envelops the room. You cannot see or breathe...\n\n\nJust before you lose consciousness, the sensation stops.\n\n\nWhatever those things were, they are gone now. You continue on, feeling rather {{TS|blue||hollow.}}</div>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Refuse}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"How disappointing...\"<br>\n{{TS||up|\"You will join us sooner or later.\"}}<br>\n{{TS|red|shake|\"HA HA HA HAHAHA!\"}}\n\nThe shapes fade away, leaving only the unnerving laughter ringing in your ears.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This event is internally called Ghosts.\n* {{C|Apparition}} is internally called Ghostly.\n* One of the few events that directly refer to [[Neow]], this event reveals she is female.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3199":{"pageid":3199,"ns":0,"title":"Designer In-Spire","revisions":[{"revid":55415,"parentid":54562,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Designer In-Spire\n|Image=Event-Designer.png\n}}\n{{E|Designer In-Spire}} is a {{QueryLink|Events|shrine:Yes|shrine Event}} found in [[Act 2]] and [[Act 3]]. It will only appear if the player has at least 75 [[Gold]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Adjustments}} {{TS|negative||Lose 40}} {{asc|15|(50)}} [[Gold]]{{TS|negative||.}} {{TS|positive||One of the following rewards appears.}}\n* {{TS|positive||[[Upgrade]] a card.}}\n* {{TS|positive||[[Upgrade]] two random cards.}}\n<br>\n{{Frame|Clean Up}} {{TS|negative||Lose 60}} {{asc|15|(75)}} [[Gold]]{{TS|negative||.}} {{TS|positive||One of the following rewards appears.}}\n* {{TS|positive||Remove a card.}}\n* {{TS|positive||[[Transform]] two cards.}}\n<br>\n{{Frame|Full Service}} {{TS|negative||Lose 90}} {{asc|15|(110)}} [[Gold]]{{TS|negative||.}}  {{TS|positive||Remove a card, then [[upgrade]] a random card.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Punch}} {{TS|negative||Lose 3}} {{asc|15|(5)}} {{TS|negative||HP.}}\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou discover a {{TS|green|up|colorful}} shop with the banner \"IN-SPIRE\" and walk in to see what's inside.<br>\n\"No, no way. Nope. Can't let you in!\" <br>\n\nA man with ridiculous clothing appears at the entrance to bar you.\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<br>\n<br>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"This will not do, no no. What is this style? {{TS||shake|Disgusting!}} Are you {{TS|negative||bleeeeding?}} {{TS|purple|up|Groooss.}} {{TS||shake|Business??}} You a customer? Fine. {{TS||up|Whaaatever.\"}} <br>\nHe lets out an exaggerated sigh and points at a list of services. <br>\n\nThe services seem fine, but you would rather punch this smug man in his smug face.\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Adjustments}}, {{Frame|Clean Up}}, and {{Frame|Full Service}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Okay, bye bye now.\" <br>\n\n...should've punched him.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Punch}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou punch him so hard your fist hurts. <br>\n\"My {{TS||shake|FACE!!}} Now I'll have to-\" <br>\n\nHe fainted. Who's {{TS|purple|up|groooss}} and {{TS|negative||bleeeeding}} now?\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* This event is internally called <code>Designer</code>.\n* If {{Frame|Punch}} is chosen, the Designer's portrait will change. This is the only [[Events|Event]] that changes its portrait.\n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:row; gap:10px; margin:0 0 10px 10px;\">\n[[File:DesignerPunched2.jpg|200px|thumb|The Designer after getting punched.]]\n</div>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.0: The Watcher'''\n** The Designer event's options are now seeded.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** Hotfix: The Designer event now has invalid options greyed out (caused softlock).\n** Added City/Beyond Event: Designer In-Spire.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3192":{"pageid":3192,"ns":0,"title":"Falling","revisions":[{"revid":55427,"parentid":54566,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Falling\n|Image=Event-Falling.png\n}}\n{{E|Falling}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 3]]. \n\n== Options ==\nAll options will randomly choose a card in the player's deck of a particular type. The option's text will explicitly tell the player which card they would lose. If the player lacks a card of a particular type, then the option relating to that type will be locked (e.g. if the player has no {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Powers}} for the {{Frame|Channel}} option, it is replaced with the option {{Frame|Locked}} Requires: Power Card).\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Land}} {{TS|negative||Lose <i>(a random</i>}} ''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}''{{TS|negative||<i>)</i>}}\n* Cannot be a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} targeted by {{R|Bottled Lightning}}.\n\n{{Frame|Channel}} {{TS|negative||Lose <i>(a random</i>}} ''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}}''{{TS|negative||<i>)</i>}}\n* Cannot be a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} targeted by {{R|Bottled Tornado}}.\n\n{{Frame|Strike}} {{TS|negative||Lose <i>(a random</i>}} ''{{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}}''{{TS|negative||<i>)</i>}}\n* Cannot be an {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} targeted by {{R|Bottled Flame}}.\n\nIf the player somehow manages to lack even a single eligible card (e.g. they have a very small deck containing only bottled cards), then the only option listed is a special {{Frame|Land}} option that has no description.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote>\n<i>As you head upwards hopping from one floating shape to another, you slip</i><br>\n<i>You begin to fall.</i><br><br>\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<br><br>\n<i>While in  free fall you consider your options:</i><br>\n<i>Land safely with your greatest techniques.</i><br>\n<i>Channel a Power to survive the fall.</i><br>\n<i>Strike at the wall to hang on to it.</i><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Land}}\n<blockquote><i>\nYou land with extreme grace before continuing on.\n</i></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Channel}}\n<blockquote><i>\nHarnessing and expending some of your raw power, you manage to land unhurt.\n</i></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Strike}}\n<blockquote><i>\nYou are able to latch on to the wall, and manage to make a short hop onto another stable platform.\n</i></blockquote>\n\nThe special {{Frame|Land}} that only occurs if the player's deck has no cards that are eligible for removal;\n<blockquote><i>\nYou seem to fall as slow as a feather, reaching the bottom without a scratch.\n</i></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Events: Falling, Secret Portal, Knowing Skull, Golden Idol, and Scrap Ooze receive ambient BGM.\n* '''Weekly Patch 30: Skewer'''\n** Falling event will no longer softlock the game if you have no valid cards to remove\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Falling Event now correctly previews upgraded cards.\n** Falling Event's RNG is now seeded.\n* '''Weekly Patch 16: Back to Work'''\n** Falling Event now shows the chosen cards when hovering the event choices.\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Falling event can no longer target bottled cards.\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Falling Event can now hit Strikes and Defends, making the event potentially not as bad.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3185":{"pageid":3185,"ns":0,"title":"Forgotten Altar","revisions":[{"revid":55433,"parentid":54578,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Forgotten Altar\n|Image=Event-ForgottenAltar.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Bloody Idol}} {{Small Card Infobox|Decay}}\n{{E|Forgotten Altar}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. This Event is the only way to obtain {{R|Bloody Idol}}. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Offer: Golden Idol}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a special}} {{R|Bloody Idol|Relic}}{{TS|positive||.}} {{TS|negative||Lose}} {{R|Golden Idol}}{{TS|negative||.}}\n* If the player does not have {{R|Golden Idol}}, this option is replaced with {{Frame|Locked}} Requires: Golden Idol.\n\n{{Frame|Sacrifice}} {{TS|positive||Gain 5 Max HP.}} {{TS|negative||Lose X HP.}}\n* X is equal to 25% {{Asc|15|(35%)}} of the player's Max HP.\n\n{{Frame|Desecrate}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed -}}{{C|Decay}}{{TS|negative||.}}\n* {{C|Decay}} - {{KW|Unplayable}}. At the end of your turn, take 2 damage.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nIn front of you sits an altar to a forgotten god.\n<br>\nAtop the altar sits an ornate female statue with arms outstretched.\n<br>\nShe calls out to you, demanding sacrifice.\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Offer: Golden Idol}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs you gently set the idol onto the altar a {{TS|blue||cold}} wind swirls throughout the room.\n<br>\nThe arms of the statue begin to discolor and crumble.\n<br><br>\nYour {{TS|gold||golden idol}} begins to dull in color and begins bleeding from its eyes.\n<br>\nThe bleeding never ceases.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Sacrifice}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou stand on the altar and cut your wrists.\n<br>\nAs the {{TS|negative||blood}} spills out in sacrifice, the arms of the statue reach out and close around your eyes.\n<br>\nEverything goes dark.\n<br>\nYou wake up a short time later feeling a new potential surging through you.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Desecrate}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou lash out and smash the statue in front of you, breaking the magical hold the room had placed upon you.\n<br>\nA dark wail echoes all around you, and you can feel the {{TS|purple|up|cursed magic}} seep into your bones.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Golden Idol}} is only obtained from the {{E|Golden Idol}} Event.\n* If the {{R|Golden Idol}} is turned into the {{R|Bloody Idol}}, {{E|The Moai Head}} Event in Act 3 will no longer accept it as an offering.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Forgotten Altar now gives you the Max HP before damaging you. This way you won't die if the damage hits you first.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Forgotten altar displays correct HP loss for the Silent now.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3167":{"pageid":3167,"ns":0,"title":"Golden Idol (Event)","revisions":[{"revid":55436,"parentid":54552,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Ambox\n| color = brown\n| icon = Necronomicon.png\n| message = ''This is information about the Event called '''Golden Idol''' in Slay the Spire. For the Golden Shrine event, see [[Golden Shrine]]. For the relic of the same name, see [[Golden Idol (Relic)]].''}}\n{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Golden Idol\n|Image=Event-GoldenIdol.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Golden Idol}} {{Small Card Infobox|Injury}}\n{{E|Golden Idol}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 1]].  It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Take}} {{TS|positive||Obtain}} {{R|Golden Idol}}{{TS|positive||.}} {{TS|negative||Trigger a trap.}}\n<blockquote>\n{{Frame|Outrun}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed -}} {{C|Injury}}{{TS|negative||.}}\n\n{{Frame|Smash}} {{TS|negative||Take X Damage.}}\n* X is equal to 25% {{Asc|15|(35%)}} of the player's Max HP.\n\n{{Frame|Hide}} {{TS|negative||Lose X Max HP.}}\n* X is equal to 8% {{Asc|15|(10%)}} of the player's Max HP.\n</blockquote>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou come across an inconspicuous pedestal with a {{TS|gold||shining gold idol}} sitting peacefully atop. It looks incredibly valuable.<br>\n<br>\nYou sure don't see any traps nearby.\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Take}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs you grab the Idol and stow it away, a giant boulder smashes through the ceiling into the ground next to you.\n<br>\nYou realize that the floor is slanted downwards as the boulder starts to roll towards you.\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Outrun}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||shake|RUUUUUUUUUUN!}}\n<br>\nYou barely leap into a side passageway as the boulder rushes by.\n<br>\nUnfortunately it feels like you sprained something however.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Smash}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou throw yourself at the boulder with everything you have. When the dust clears, you can make a safe way out.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Hide}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||shake|SQUISH!}}\n<br>\nThe boulder flattens you a little as it passes by, but otherwise you can get out of here.\n</div></blockquote></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nIf there was ever an obvious trap, this would be it.\n<br>\nYou decide not to interfere with objects placed upon pedestals.\n</div></blockquote></blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{E|Forgotten Altar}} will allow {{R|Golden Idol}} to be exchanged for {{R|Bloody Idol}}.\n* {{E|The Moai Head}} will allow {{R|Golden Idol}} to be exchanged for 333 [[Gold]].\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The Idol's appearance and the boulder trap are both references to ''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raiders_of_the_Lost_Ark Raiders of the Lost Ark]'', an ''Indiana Jones'' movie.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Events: Falling, Secret Portal, Knowing Skull, Golden Idol, and Scrap Ooze receive ambient BGM.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 7: Setting Up All the Things'''\n** Golden Idol Event options are slightly harsher. 20% -> 25% damage and 5% -> 8% Max HP loss.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3060":{"pageid":3060,"ns":0,"title":"Golden Shrine","revisions":[{"revid":54540,"parentid":35667,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Golden Shrine\n|Image=Event-GoldenShrine.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Regret}}\n{{E|Golden Shrine}} is a {{QueryLink|Events|shrine:Yes|shrine Event}} encountered in all [[Acts]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Pray}} {{TS|positive||Gain 100 Gold.}}\n\n{{Frame|Desecrate}} {{TS|positive||Gain 275 Gold.}} {{TS|negative||Become Cursed -}} {{C|Regret}}.\n* {{C|Regret}} - {{KW|Unplayable}}. At the end of your turn, lose HP equal to the number of cards in your hand.\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nBefore you lies an elaborate shrine to an ancient spirit.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Pray}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs your hand touches the shrine, {{TS|gold||gold}} rains from the ceiling {{TS||up|showering you in riches.}}\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Desecrate}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nEach time you strike the shrine, {{TS|gold||gold}} pours forth again and again! <br>\n\nAs you pocket the riches, something {{TS|negative||weighs heavily on you.}}\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou ignore the shrine.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3193":{"pageid":3193,"ns":0,"title":"Old Beggar","revisions":[{"revid":55472,"parentid":54580,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Old Beggar\n|Image=Event-Beggar.png\n}}\n{{E|Old Beggar}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. It will only appear if the player has at least 75 [[Gold]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Offer Gold}} {{TS|gold||75 [[Gold]]:}} {{TS|positive||Remove a card from your deck.}} \n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAn old beggar cloaked in fur reaches his hands out towards you as you pass. \"Spare some coin, child?\"\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Offer Gold}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe beggar takes off its cloak to reveal that he is {{TS|blue||Cleric!}} <br>\n{{TS||shake|\"You are a kind soul. Receive my purification!\"}} he screams. <br>\nYou are unsure if he is grateful or mad.\n</div><br><br>\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote>\nIf the player returns from the Map screen instead of progressing to the next floor, the event has extra dialogue:\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\"><br><br>\n{{TS||shake|\"I hope you do better this time, friend!\"}} he shouts.\n<br>\nWondering what was implied by this, you push forward.\n</div></blockquote></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe beggar looks to the floor as you pass. <br>\n\"You will never make a difference... You never do.\"\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Cleric is also encountered in {{E|The Cleric}} event.\n* {{R|Face of Cleric}} from the {{E|Face Trader}} event references Cleric. There is no special dialogue if the player encounters Cleric while owning his face.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** You no longer run into The Cleric or Beggar events if you do not have enough gold.\n* '''Weekly Patch 15: Surprise Patch'''\n** Beggar Event now correctly displays the tip for what you are choosing for the card selection screen.\n* '''Weekly Patch 6: We're Back!'''\n** Fixed typo for Cleric event. Wandering -> Wondering.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3177":{"pageid":3177,"ns":0,"title":"Secret Portal","revisions":[{"revid":55493,"parentid":54573,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Secret Portal\n|Image=Event-SecretPortal.png\n}}\n{{E|Secret Portal}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in [[Act 3]]. It will only appear if 800 seconds (13 minutes and 20 seconds) have passed.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Enter the Portal}} IMMEDIATELY travel to [[Bosses#Act 3 Bosses|the boss]].\n* The player is put directly into combat with the [[Bosses#Act 3 Bosses|Act 3 boss]] at the end of the act.\n<br>\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nBefore you is a sight that seems out of place in the alien landscape around you. Strangely placed into one of the living walls of the Beyond is an enclosed stone entrance filled with a {{TS|purple|up|swirling magical portal.}}\n<br>\n<br>\nYou aren't sure where it leads, but maybe it could speed your journey through the Spire.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Enter the Portal}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nJumping through the portal, your sense of time and space is completely torn apart.\n<br>\n<br>\nAs you reorient yourself to the new surroundings, you realize that right before you is a fearsome battle.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nCareful and cautious seems the better approach for reaching the top of the Spire. Ignoring the portal you continue on.\n</div> </blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* Apart from the unusual method of entering the boss floor and skipping the rest of Act 3, entering the portal is otherwise a completely normal boss fight.\n** {{R|Pantograph}} and {{R|Slaver's Collar}} trigger as expected.\n** There will still be the {{Asc|20|double boss afterwards on A20}}.\n** Defeating the boss {{Asc|20|(or both bosses)}} will still allow the player to enter [[Acts#Act 4: The Ending|Act 4]] if they have all required [[Mechanics#Keys|Keys]]. Although, the player should be careful to collect the Ruby Key from a [[Rest Site]] prior to the event since they will skip the guaranteed [[Rest Site]] before the boss (which is often relied on as the last opportunity to collect the Ruby Key).\n* The player's current floor is only increased by 1, which causes them to fight the [[Bosses#Act 3 Bosses|Act 3 Boss]] earlier than the usual floor 50.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The 800 second minimum time limit in order to encounter this event was implemented after some discussion with the Slay the Spire speedrunning community during the game's development. Without the limit, the fastest winning runs relied on encountering {{E|Secret Portal}} to skip many floors of Act 3. This would offer such an enormous time save that runs which didn't manage to find {{E|Secret Portal}} early enough could never beat runs that did. This requirement means that no speedrun would be able to encounter {{E|Secret Portal}}, while casual runs under normal gameplay would easily satisfy the minimum time requirement and be able to encounter the event as intended.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Secret Portal event no longer says Ignored in run history. Run history rows capped at 20 elements.\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Events: Falling, Secret Portal, Knowing Skull, Golden Idol, and Scrap Ooze receive ambient BGM.\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** New Event (Beyond): Secret Portal.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3205":{"pageid":3205,"ns":0,"title":"The Colosseum","revisions":[{"revid":55509,"parentid":54582,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Colosseum\n|Image=Event-Colosseum.png\n}}\n{{E|The Colosseum}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}. It only appears after the guaranteed [[Map Locations#Treasure Room|Treasure Room]] on the 6th floor of the City.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Fight}}\n* The player enters a fight with a {{M|Blue Slaver}} and {{M|Red Slaver}}. This fight gives no rewards.\n<blockquote>\nAfter the fight ends, a choice has to be made: \n\n{{Frame|COWARDICE}} Escape.\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|VICTORY}} A powerful fight with many rewards.\n* The player enters a fight with {{M|Taskmaster}} and {{M|Gremlin Nob}}.\n* The rewards are 100 [[Gold]], 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]], 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]], a card reward, and sometimes a [[Potion]].\n</blockquote>\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||shake|Thwack!!!}} <br>\n.. <br>\n...... <br>\n... <br>\n{{TS||up|You were knocked unconscious...}}\n</div> <br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n<br><br>\n\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||up|Groggy}} and with a {{TS||shake|throbbing}} head, you awaken to find yourself thrown in the center of a massive stadium with an overflowing audience of {{TS|blue||Slavers,}} {{TS|purple||Cultists,}} and other denizens of the City! <br>\n\nAn armored giant with a {{TS|gold||golden crown}} bellows at you from atop, <br>\n{{TS||shake|\"WE NOW BEGIN THE 4200TH COMBAT!!!!\"}} <br>\nA gate on the opposite side opens...\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Fight}}\n<blockquote>\n(The player enters combat with a {{M|Blue Slaver}} and {{M|Red Slaver}}. After ending the fight, more dialogue is presented.)<br>\n<br>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS||shake|\"WELL DONE, WEAKLING!\"}} <br>\nThe giant mock claps whilst he riles up the crowd with exaggerated gestures. <br>\n{{TS|gold|up|Gold}} {{TS||up|and}} {{TS|gold|up|confetti}} {{TS||up|shower you!}} <br>\n{{TS||shake|\"TIME FOR THE REAL CHALLENGE!!\"}} <br>\n<br>\nThe last battle left a small hole in the Colosseum's wall, you can easily escape through there while everyone is distracted. <br>\nDo you stay and fight?\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|COWARDICE}}\n<blockquote>\n(No dialogue)\n</blockquote>\n{{Frame|VICTORY}}\n<blockquote>\n(No dialogue, the player enters combat with {{M|Taskmaster}} and {{M|Gremlin Nob}})\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\nSome mechanics behave strangely during the two fights in this event due to their atypical nature:\n* {{Frame|Fight}} is treated as a normal combat.\n** {{P|Smoke Bomb}} can be used to escape the fight and the player will still be prompted to choose either {{Frame|COWARDICE}} or {{Frame|VICTORY}} afterwards as normal.\n** The game still rolls to drop a [[Potion]], but never presents the player with it even if a [[Potion]] would be dropped. This means it is impossible to know if the [[Potions#Sources|potion chance]] has increased or decreased, and this uncertainty will persist until the [[Potions#Sources|potion chance]] resets at start of the next act.\n** While it has no combat rewards and transitions to the next dialogue of the event very quickly, end-of-combat effects like {{R|Burning Blood}} and {{C|Self Repair}} will still trigger.\n* {{Frame|VICTORY}} is treated as an [[Elite]] combat for ''most'' effects.\n** {{R|Preserved Insect}}, {{R|Sling of Courage}}, and {{R|Slaver's Collar}} will all trigger their effects as expected.\n** The only exception is {{R|Black Star}}, which has no effect on the [[Relics]] dropped as rewards. This combat will ''always'' drop exactly 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Rare|Rare}} [[Relic]] and 1 {{QueryLink|Relics|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} [[Relic]].\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The \"armored giant with a {{TS|gold||golden crown}}\" is likely {{M|The Champ}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Colosseum event now appears only at the top half of Act 2.\n* '''Slay the Spire 1.0: Farewell Early Access'''\n** Colossuem Nob fight ordering swapped so that the Nob can apply Vulnerable.\n* '''Weekly Patch 56: The Collector'''\n** Colosseum event's second fight is now a Gremlin Nob + Taskmaster (rather than 2 Gremlin Nobs)\n* '''Weekly Patch 42: Reboot'''\n** Orb VFX no longer render in the background of the Colosseum event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 41: Chill'''\n** Colosseum Nobs no longer play double music.\n** Fixed bug causing block to maintain between colosseum combats.\n** Fixed Smoke Bomb and Colosseum bug that caused the player to go invisible.\n** Killing a Colosseum Nob no longer causes the music to stop.\n* '''Weekly Patch 39: We Meet Again!'''\n** Added City Event: The Colosseum.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3065":{"pageid":3065,"ns":0,"title":"The Divine Fountain","revisions":[{"revid":55975,"parentid":54544,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Divine Fountain\n|Image=Event-DivineFountain.png\n}}\n{{E|The Divine Fountain}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in all [[Acts]]. This event can only appear if you have a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curse}} in your deck.\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Drink}} {{TS|positive||Remove all}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Curse|Curses}} {{TS|positive||from your deck.}}\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou come across {{TS|blue|up|shimmering water}} flowing endlessly from a fountain on a nearby wall.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Drink}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs you drink the {{TS|blue|up|water,}} you feel a {{TS|purple||dark grasp}} loosen.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nUnsure of the nature of this water, you continue on your way, parched.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* Removing all Curses may not be beneficial if you are relying on the {{BD|Strength}} from {{R|Du-Vu Doll}}.\n* The Max HP gain from {{R|Darkstone Periapt}} is kept even when the Curses are removed.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3171":{"pageid":3171,"ns":0,"title":"The Joust","revisions":[{"revid":55510,"parentid":54565,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Joust\n|Image=Event-Joust.png\n}}\n{{E|The Joust}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in [[Act 2]]. This event can only be encountered with more than 50 [[Gold]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Murderer}} {{TS|gold||Bet 50 Gold}} - {{TS|positive||70%: win 100 Gold.}}\n\n{{Frame|Owner}} {{TS|gold||Bet 50 Gold}} - {{TS|positive||30%: win 250 Gold.}}\n\nThere is no option to avoid betting.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs you make your way through the large buildings you come across a long narrow bridge and spot knights on either side, facing one another. <br>\nYou approach... <br>\n{{TS||shake|\"HALT!\"}} <br>\n\nA knight forcefully gestures you to stop with its giant lance.\n</div><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Continue}}\n\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Today is the day I must settle the score with the {{TS|negative||murderer}} of my beloved pet, {{TS|gold||Noodles.}} Until then, you may not pass. <br>\n\nFellow witness, why don't you {{TS|blue||bet}} on who you think will emerge victorious?\"\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Murderer}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"I can't believe you're betting against {{TS|gold||Noodles!\"}} <br>\n\nFurious, he clamps down his helmet and rushes towards his nemesis.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Owner}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Give me strength, {{TS|gold||Noodles!\"}} <br>\n\nClamping down his helmet, the knight charges forward.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS|gold|shake|* CRASH!!!* }} {{TS|negative|shake|* KLAAAANG!* }} <br>\n\n{{TS|green|shake|* POW!* }}\n</div></blockquote>\n\n<blockquote>\n'''Depending on who loses the joust:''' <i>The owner died. / The nemesis was slain.</i>\n<br>\n<br>\n\n'''When losing the bet:'''\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">You {{TS|negative||lost}} the bet, but at least you weren't gouged by a lance.</div>\n\n'''When winning the bet:'''\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">You {{TS|green||win}} the bet. Unsure what to think, you grab your winnings and leave.</div>\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* If the player possesses {{R|Ectoplasm}}, this event is a mandatory loss of 50 [[Gold]]. There is no option to leave the event without betting, and any potential winnings cannot be gained.\n* The player may consider using the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expected_value expected value] (EV) of each option to determine who they want to bet on.\n** The EV of betting on the Murderer is a net increase of 20 [[Gold]] (a 70% chance to receive 100 [[Gold]] is an expected 70 [[Gold]], minus the 50 [[Gold]] that was bet. <code>0.7 x 100 - 50 = 20</code>)\n** The EV of betting on the Owner is a net increase of 25 [[Gold]] (a 30% chance to receive 250 [[Gold]] is an expected 75 [[Gold]], minus the 50 [[Gold]] that was bet. <code>0.3 x 250 - 50 = 25</code>)\n** It may be more beneficial to ignore the EV and instead consider whether the relatively safe 50 extra [[Gold]] by betting on the Murderer is more useful to the player's current run compared to risking the bet on the Owner and likely losing their 50 [[Gold]] for the more unlikely net gain of 200 [[Gold]].\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 21: Channel Lightning'''\n** Seeds are now utilized for The Joust event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** Joust event now has correct wording for some incorrect options.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3183":{"pageid":3183,"ns":0,"title":"The Library","revisions":[{"revid":55450,"parentid":54583,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Library\n|Image=Event-Library.png\n}}\n{{E|The Library}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Read}} {{TS|positive||Choose 1 of 20 cards to add to your deck.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Sleep}} {{TS|positive||Heal X HP.}}\n* X is equal to 33% {{Asc|15|(20%)}} of the player's Max HP.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou come across an ornate building which appears abandoned. <br>\nA plaque that has been torn free from a wall is on the floor. It reads, {{TS|blue||\"THE LIBRARY\".}} <br>\nInside, you find countless rows of scrolls, manuscripts, and books. <br>\nYou pick one and cozy yourself into a chair for some quiet time.\n</div><br>\n\n{{Frame|Read}}\n\nThere are 3 possible stories that the player can read. One of the following is chosen at random.\n\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe story is about an insect-controlling teenage girl who aspires to become a hero. The book is filled with creative uses of power, combat strategies, and varying perspectives.<br><br>\nSatisfying.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe story is about a man who journeyed beyond the stars and found himself stuck on a desolate foreign planet. Ingenuity, luck, perseverance, and humor to retain his sanity were his tools to return home.<br><br>\nFascinating.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe story takes place in a giant isolated building underground as the outside conditions have become unbearable. The novel is mired with conspiracies, propaganda, and injustice. You ponder if similar dynamics are at play within the Spire.<br><br>\nUnsettling.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Sleep}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nReading is for chumps. <br>\nYou doze off in a comfy chair instead. <br>\n{{TS||up|Zzz... zzz... ..Zz...}} <br>\nYou wake up feeling refreshed.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{Frame|Sleep}} is unaffected by {{R|Regal Pillow}}, does not trigger {{R|Dream Catcher}}, and can still be chosen with {{R|Coffee Dripper}}.\n* {{R|Mark of the Bloom}} makes {{Frame|Sleep}} serve only as a way to skip adding a card to your deck as it will no longer heal you.\n* {{R|N'loth's Gift}} increases the likelihood of each card offered by {{Frame|Read}} being {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Each of the stories that can be randomly chosen when {{Frame|Read}} is selected are references to real-world books. They are:\n** [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worm_(web_serial) Worm, by John C. McCrae]. Referenced by the story about the ''\"insect-controlling teenage girl\"''.\n** [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Martian_(Weir_novel) The Martian, by Andy Weir]. Referenced by the story about the ''\"man who journeyed beyond the stars\"''.\n** [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silo_(series) Wool, by Hugh Howey]. Referenced by the story about the ''\"giant isolated building underground\"''.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Library event can no longer contain duplicate cards.\n* '''Weekly Patch 53: Blizzard'''\n** Fix for Egg relics causing an issue with cards in the Library event screen.\n* '''Weekly Patch 18: Paranormal'''\n** Fix for Calling Bell/Library/Pandora's Box exploit.\n* '''Weekly Patch 16: Back to Work'''\n** You can now view your deck or the map when the grid card select screen is up (Such as The Library event)\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Insect-controlling -> typo in The Library event's text.\n* '''Weekly Patch 2: Slimes!'''\n** Updating The Library event's option to clarify that you choose 1 of 20 cards rather than the usual 3.\n* '''Day 1 Patch'''\n** Minor wording updates for Library event.\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3184":{"pageid":3184,"ns":0,"title":"The Nest","revisions":[{"revid":55513,"parentid":54585,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Nest\n|Image=Event-TheNest.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Ritual Dagger}}\n{{E|The Nest}} is an event found exclusively in [[Act 2]]. It is one of the events affected by {{Asc|15|Ascension}}.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Smash and Grab}} {{TS|positive||Obtain 99 {{Asc|15|(50)}} Gold.}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Stay in Line}} {{TS|positive||Obtain {{C|Ritual Dagger}}.}} {{TS|negative||Lose 6 HP.}}\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nA long line of {{TS|blue|up|hooded figures}} can be seen entering an {{TS|purple||unassuming cathedral.}}\n</div><br>\n<div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nNaturally, you join the line and are quickly surrounded by {{TS|negative||Cultists!}} <br>\nThey ignore you as they gleefully {{TS||shake|chant}} and {{TS||up|wave}} their weapons around. <br>\n\n{{TS|negative|shake|\"MURDER!! MURDER MURDER!!\"}} <br>\n{{TS|blue|up|\"CAW CAW CAAAAAWWW!\"}} <br>\n{{TS|negative|shake|\"MURDER! MURDER MURDER!!\"}} <br>\n{{TS|blue|up|\"CAAW CAW CAAAAAAWW!!\"}} <br>\n\nYou eye a {{TS|gold||Donation Box...}}\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Smash and Grab}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThey didn't even notice.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Stay in Line}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou decide to stay in line (out of fear) to see what will happen. <br>\n\nEventually, you are face-to-face with the leader. A well-dressed cultist hands you an {{TS|gold||Ornate Dagger.}} Like the others before you, you slash your forearm and let the blood drip into a misshapen bowl. <br>\n\nThe cultists {{TS||shake|chant}} and {{TS||shake|holler}} for you! <br>\n\n{{TS|blue|up|\"CAAW CAW CAAAAAAWW!!\"}} <br>\n\nYou chant, too. Why not?\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* {{E|The Nest}} depicts many aspects of the cult of the {{M|Awakened One}} that is encountered throughout the Spire. The {{M|Cultist|Cultists}} waiting in line, the \"well-dressed cultist\" could be a {{M|Chosen}}, and the {{C|Ritual Dagger}} is identical to the one that can be seen sticking out of the {{M|Awakened One}}'s chest.\n* Internally called <code>Nest</code>.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** an -> a typo in the Nest event.\n* '''Weekly Patch 29: TURBO'''\n** In the Nest event, you receive the dagger for 6 damage instead of a downgrade now.\n** In the Nest event, the non-dagger option steals less gold now (150 -> 99). Ascension 15 -> 50.\n* '''Weekly Patch 28: The Ritual'''\n** New Act 2 event: The Nest\n** New Card: Ritual Dagger\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3066":{"pageid":3066,"ns":0,"title":"The Woman in Blue","revisions":[{"revid":54545,"parentid":35693,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=The Woman in Blue\n|Image=Event-WomanInBlue.png\n}}\n{{E|The Woman in Blue}} is a shrine [[Event]] encountered in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Buy 1 Potion}} {{TS|gold||20 Gold.}}\n\n{{Frame|Buy 2 Potions}} {{TS|gold||30 Gold.}}\n\n{{Frame|Buy 3 Potions}} {{TS|gold||40 Gold.}}\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nFrom the darkness, an arm pulls you into a small shop. As your eyes adjust, you see a pale woman in sharp clothes gesturing to a wall of potions. <br>\n\"Buy a potion. Now!\" she states.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Buy}} any amount of potions\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n\"Good. Now leave.\" <br>\nYou exit the shop cautiously.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\n{{TS|negative|shake|WHAM}} <br>\nHer gloved fist collides with your face, nearly knocking you off your feet. <br>\n\"Get out before I litter the floor with your guts.\" You take her word and exit with your guts still safely in your body.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* Even if you skip grabbing the potions you bought, she will still be satisfied.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3175":{"pageid":3175,"ns":0,"title":"Tomb of Lord Red Mask","revisions":[{"revid":55514,"parentid":54571,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Tomb of Lord Red Mask\n|Image=Event-RedMaskTomb.png\n}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Red Mask}}\n{{E|Tomb of Lord Red Mask}} is an [[Event]] found in [[Act 3]].\n\n== Options ==\n=== If The Player Owns {{R|Red Mask}} ===\n{{Frame|Don the Red Mask}} {{TS|positive||Gain 222 [[Gold]].}}\n* The player gets to keep {{R|Red Mask}} afterwards. The [[Gold]] is purely a reward for owning the relic.\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens. \n<br>\n<br>\n\n=== If The Player Does Not Own {{R|Red Mask}} ===\n{{Frame|Locked}} Requires: {{R|Red Mask}}\n<br>\n<br>\n{{Frame|Offer: X Gold}} {{TS|negative||Lose all [[Gold]].}} {{TS|positive||Obtain a Relic.}}\n* X is equal to all of the player's [[Gold]].\n* Rewards the player with {{R|Red Mask}}.\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens. \n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nA highly ornamented tomb can be seen on the other side of a floating path. Upon reaching the tomb, you notice a slot for {{TS|gold||gold}} coins with a scratched out inscription above it.\n</div> \n\n{{Frame|Don the Red Mask}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou don the mask and the tomb starts to {{TS||up|flake away...}} a secret passage!<br>\n<br>\nThe passage is lined with countless stolen goods and mounds of {{TS|gold||gold!}}\n</div> </blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Offer: X Gold}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAn opening appears in the tomb and out slides a small red mask with a note attached. \"Take from others as I have taken from you!\"\n</div> </blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote>\n(No dialogue)\n</blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Notes ==\n* {{R|Red Mask}} is obtained from the [[Act 2]] event {{E|Masked Bandits}}.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3067":{"pageid":3067,"ns":0,"title":"Transmogrifier","revisions":[{"revid":54546,"parentid":35694,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Transmogrifier\n|Image=Event-Transmogrifier.png\n}}\n{{E|Transmogrifier}} is a shrine [[Event]] encountered in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Pray}} {{KW|Transform}} {{TS|positive||a card.}}\n* Read more on Transform rules [[Transform#Rules|here]].\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nBefore you lies an elaborate shrine to a forgotten spirit.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Pray}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nAs the power of the shrine flows through you, your mind feels altered.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou ignore the shrine.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Internally called <code>Transmorgrifier</code> where it's misspelled with an extra '''r''' before the '''g'''.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"3068":{"pageid":3068,"ns":0,"title":"Upgrade Shrine","revisions":[{"revid":54547,"parentid":35696,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Upgrade Shrine\n|Image=Event-UpgradeShrine.png\n}}\n{{E|Upgrade Shrine}} is a shrine [[Event]] found in all [[Acts]].\n\nShrine events appear less frequently than other events.\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Pray}} {{KW|Upgrade}} {{TS|positive||a card.}}\n\n{{Frame|Leave}} Nothing happens.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nBefore you lies an elaborate shrine to a forgotten spirit.\n</div>\n\n{{Frame|Pray}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nThe shrine's energy flows into you, making you stronger.\n</div></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Leave}}\n<blockquote><div style=\"font-style:italic\">\nYou ignore the shrine.\n</div></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]},"2500":{"pageid":2500,"ns":0,"title":"Vampires","revisions":[{"revid":55532,"parentid":54586,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Event Infobox\n|Name=Vampires\n|Image=Event-Vampires.png\n}} {{Small Card Infobox|Bite}} {{Small Relic Infobox|Blood Vial}}\n{{E|Vampires}} is an [[Event]] found exclusively in [[Act 2]].\n\n== Options ==\n{{Frame|Offer: Blood Vial}} {{TS|negative||Lose}} {{R|Blood Vial}}{{TS|negative||.}} <span class=\"positive-text\"> Remove all</span> {{C|Strike (Ironclad)|Strikes}}{{TS|positive||.}} <span class=\"positive-text\">Receive 5</span> {{C|Bite|Bites}}{{TS|positive||.}}\n* Only present if the player has {{R|Blood Vial}}.\n\n{{Frame|Accept}} <span class=\"positive-text\">Remove all</span> {{C|Strike (Ironclad)|Strikes}}{{TS|positive||.}} <span class=\"positive-text\">Receive 5</span> {{C|Bite|Bites}}{{TS|positive||.}} <span class=\"negative-text\">Lose X Max HP.</span>\n* X is equal to 30% of the player's max HP.\n\n{{Frame|Refuse}} Nothing happens.\n\nYou are then given the option to {{Frame|Leave}}.\n\n== Dialogue ==\n<blockquote><i>\nNavigating an unlit street, you come across several hooded figures in the midst of some dark ritual. As you approach, they turn to you in eerie unison. The tallest among them bares fanged teeth and extends a long, pale hand towards you.\n<br>\n{{TS||up|\"Join us brother, and feel the warmth of the Spire.\"}}\n</i></blockquote><blockquote><br><br>\n\n{{Frame|Offer: Blood Vial}}\n<blockquote><i>\nThe pale figures gasp as you take out the {{TS|gold||Blood Vial.}}\n<br>\n{{TS||up|\"The master's blood... the master's blood!}} {{TS||shake|THE MASTER'S BLOOD!\"}}\n<br>\nThey all chant fervently as the tall one bows before you. \"Drink from His blood, and become one with {{TS|gold|up|Him.\"}}\n<br>\nThe chant growing louder, you consume the contents of the vial. Your vision immediately {{TS||up|warps}} and fades to darkness.\n<br>\n<br>\nYou wake up some time later, alone. An intense {{TS||up|hunger}} passes through your belly. You {{TS|red||must feed...}}\n</i></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Accept}}\n<blockquote><i>\nThe tall figure grabs your arm, pulls you forward, and sinks his fangs into your neck. You feel a {{TS||shake|dark force}} pour into your neck and {{TS||shake|course}} through your body.\n<br>\n...\n<br>\nYou wake up some time later, alone. An intense {{TS||up|hunger}} passes through your belly. You {{TS|red||must feed...}}\n</i></blockquote>\n\n{{Frame|Refuse}}\n<blockquote><i>\nYou step back and raise your weapon in defiance. The tall figure sighs.\n<br>\n\"Very well.\" The entire group of hooded figures morph into a thick black fog that flows away from you.\n<br>\nYou are alone once more.\n</i></blockquote>\n</blockquote>\n\n== Trivia ==\n* The ''{{TS||up|\"Join us\"}}'' line of dialogue changes depending on the player's current character.\n** For the [[Ironclad]] it reads, ''{{TS||up|\"Join us brother\"}}''.\n** For the [[Silent]] and the [[Watcher]] it reads, ''{{TS||up|\"Join us sister\"}}''.\n** For the [[Defect]] it reads, ''{{TS||up|\"Join us broken one\"}}''.\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Vampires and Council of Ghosts events now show how much Max HP is lost (rather than showing %)\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 51: Recursion'''\n** Minor text cleanup for Vampires event.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** When accepting to become a vampire, a SFX now plays.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 30: Skewer'''\n** Fix for Vampire and Ghost Council event which could set your HP to 0.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 5: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Vampires event dialog option is slightly shortened so it fits in the option.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Vampires event text now displays the correct options if you reject them.\n\n\n{{EventNav}}\n[[Category:Events]]"}}}]}}}}